 {
  "id": 4081885615,
  "type": null,
  "body": "Applying option 1 for @AlphaTechini: Hash API token secrets with a fast single-pass SHA-256 instead of hashSecret in issueToken and verifyToken, since token secrets are long random values, and keep the higher iteration count only for passwords; this leaves token secrets without key stretching, which is acceptable only because they are random. A merge request with the change follows, then a re-measure of this journey.",
  "author": {
   "id": 43692725,
   "username": "ai-downstream-gitlab-ai-hackathon",
   "public_email": null,
